# https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to the SpatialEntity it is about. Every attestation must\n        have exactly one subject entity. This is the primary entity being\n        described by the bundled name, geometry, timespan, and type assertions.\n\n        Functional property: each attestation has exactly one subject entity.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attests about"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#attests_geometry
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_geometry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_geometry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_geometry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_geometry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to a Geometry it asserts for the SpatialEntity. An\n        attestation may assert multiple geometries (e.g., point and polygon)\n        or no geometry at all (e.g., name-only attestations from textual sources).\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_geometry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attests geometry"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#attests_name
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to a Name it asserts for the SpatialEntity. An attestation\n        may assert multiple names (e.g., primary name and variants) or no name\n        at all (e.g., geometry-only attestations).\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attests name"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to a PropertyValue it asserts of the SpatialEntity — a\n        population, a valuation, an elevation, a market's trading day. An\n        attestation may assert several properties or none.\n\n        These are among the commonest things a source says about an entity, and\n        they carry exactly the provenance and temporal scoping the attestation\n        pattern exists to handle: a population figure is a claim, by a named\n        source, about one SpatialEntity, over a Timespan, with a certainty. The\n        attestation's own timespans scope the property as they scope every\n        other facet in the bundle.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_property> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attests property"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#attests_timespan
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to the Timespan during which the attested\n        properties (name, geometry, type) were applicable. Distinct from\n        the attestation's creation date: this is the historical timespan\n        being asserted, not when the assertion was made.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attests timespan"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Type> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to a Type classification it assigns to the SpatialEntity.\n        An attestation may assert multiple types or no type at all.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attests_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attests type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status
<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Citation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Whether the attribution of the evidence to the cited source was\n        stated by the source or resolved editorially. Should point to a\n        concept in a SKOS concept scheme. The starter concepts are:\n\n        - plato:AttributionStated: the source is named where the form\n          occurs. The default, and usually omitted.\n        - plato:AttributionInferred: the source was given as 'ibidem' or\n          'idem' and resolved by an editor, so the attribution is inferred\n          rather than stated. Not marginal: about one attestation in twenty\n          in the English Place-Name Society corpus.\n\n        A statement about the citation, not about the form, which is why it\n        lives here and not in plato:occurrence_context.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#attribution_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attribution status"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_candidate
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_candidate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_candidate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Candidate> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_candidate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_candidate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "candidate entity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_source
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Candidate> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#candidate_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "source entity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#cites
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Citation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The Authority (a Source or a Dataset) this Citation uses. Exactly one\n        per Citation: an attestation resting on two sources has two\n        Citations.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#cites> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "cites"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contains_attestation
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_attestation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Gazetteer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a Gazetteer to an Attestation contributed within it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contains attestation"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Gazetteer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a Gazetteer to a SpatialEntity it contains."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contains_entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contains entity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributed_by
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributed_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributed_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributed_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributed_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The agent (person, team, or process) who created this attestation.\n\n        Semantically equivalent to PROV-O's prov:wasAttributedTo for provenance\n        tracking. We don't use formal rdfs:subPropertyOf to avoid importing\n        PROV-O's domain/range constraints. Distinct from sourced_by, which\n        indicates the historical source being cited.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributed_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contributed by"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Organization> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Organizational affiliation of the contributor. Links to a\n        plato:Organization entity, which can be further described using\n        FOAF, schema.org, or other ontology properties. Organizations\n        should ideally use persistent identifiers (ROR, ISNI, etc.).\n\n        For simple cases, use contributor_affiliation_string for free-text\n        affiliation names.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "affiliation"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from
<https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        This Source is a copy, transcript, edition, calendar or confirmation\n        of that one. A later cartulary copy of a charter, an inspeximus, or a\n        printed edition of a manuscript is a Source of its own, with its own\n        source_timespan, derived_from the document it transmits. An\n        attestation should cite the Source it was actually read in; the chain\n        of derived_from links records what that Source transmits. The kind of\n        derivation (copy, edition, calendar, inspeximus) is not yet\n        distinguished; a sub-property or a small vocabulary can be added when\n        a project needs it.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#derived_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "derived from"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#form_status
<https://w3id.org/plato#form_status> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#form_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#form_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#form_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The status of the name form this attestation contributes: read in the\n        cited source, chosen by the cited authority, or derived by the\n        contributing project. Should point to a concept in a SKOS concept\n        scheme. The starter concepts are:\n\n        - plato:Attested: a form read in the cited source. The default, and\n          usually omitted.\n        - plato:Headword: the editorial or preferred form under which the\n          cited authority files the entry ('Bunsty Hundred'). A scholarly\n          decision rather than a reading, and typically the form users search\n          for. Another authority may choose differently, which is why it is a\n          sourced attestation and not a label on the SpatialEntity.\n        - plato:Normalised: a form derived from an attested one for matching\n          or search ('Bunstow(e)' resolved to 'Bunstowe'), attested by no\n          source and carrying no independent evidential value. It may point\n          to the attestation it was derived from through a meta-attestation.\n        - plato:Reconstructed: a form inferred but not attested, the\n          philologists' asterisked form.\n\n        A different axis from plato:name_type, which classifies what the name\n        denotes: a headword is still a toponym. It sits on the Attestation,\n        not on the Name, because the same string can be a reading in one\n        attestation and a headword in another. The WHG ingestion prototype\n        reached the same placement independently: its preferred-name flag is\n        on the attestation, not on the toponym record.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#form_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "form status"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_owner
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_owner> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Gazetteer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "owner"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#geometry_role
<https://w3id.org/plato#geometry_role> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geometry_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geometry_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geometry_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        What this geometry depicts, as distinct from how precisely it is known\n        (plato:spatial_precision) or where its indexing point falls\n        (plato:repr_point). A SpatialEntity may be attested with several geometries at\n        once — a built extent, the location of a specific central feature, a\n        proxy standing in for the whole, the anchor of a map label — and without\n        a declared role a consumer cannot tell them apart, nor state which one\n        an analysis used.\n\n        Should point to a concept in a SKOS concept scheme (e.g. plato:Extent,\n        plato:FeaturePoint, plato:RepresentativePoint, plato:LabelAnchor,\n        plato:Itinerary). Using URIs rather than free text lets gazetteers that\n        record geometry differently be compared.\n\n        Note that role is orthogonal to precision: a proxy locator may be\n        surveyed to the metre and still not depict the SpatialEntity it stands for. A\n        parish church's coordinates contributed as a locator for a town are a\n        representative point of high precision, not an imprecise feature point.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geometry_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "geometry role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Citation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to a Citation: its qualified use of one\n        Authority, with a locator and an attribution status. An attestation\n        may have several, one per source it rests on.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has citation"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The nature of a meta-attestation's relationship to its target attestation.\n        Should reference a controlled vocabulary concept defining the relationship\n        type. Standard values include:\n\n        - 'contradicts': asserts the target attestation is incorrect\n        - 'supports': provides additional evidence for the target attestation\n        - 'supersedes': replaces the target attestation with newer information\n        - 'refines': provides more precise information than the target\n        - 'challenges': questions the target attestation's validity\n        - 'bundles': groups the target with other related attestations\n\n        Using SKOS concepts rather than strings enables vocabulary management\n        and multilingual labels.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_meta_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "meta-attestation type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#has_relation_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_relation_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_relation_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_relation_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_relation_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Specifies the semantic type of a entity-to-entity relationship\n        attested by an Attestation. References a RelationType authority\n        which defines the relationship's label, inverse, and domain/range\n        constraints. Examples: 'capital_of', 'successor_to',\n        'connected_by_trade_route_to'.\n\n        The extensible vocabulary pattern allows new relationship types to\n        be added as Authority records without modifying the ontology.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_relation_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has relation type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Period> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links a Period authority to its temporal extent, represented as a\n        Timespan node. Used for locally-defined periods or when more detailed\n        temporal modeling is needed than provided by external period definitions.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#has_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has timespan"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#hull
<https://w3id.org/plato#hull> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#hull> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#hull> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_by
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The agent who made or confirmed this identity assertion."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "asserted by"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The second SpatialEntity in an identity assertion."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identity object"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_sourced_by
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The Authority (Source or Dataset) that provides evidence for\n        this identity assertion, if any.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identity sourced by"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_subject
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_subject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The first SpatialEntity in an identity assertion."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identity subject"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#member_of_group
<https://w3id.org/plato#member_of_group> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#member_of_group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Gazetteer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#member_of_group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#GazetteerGroup> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#member_of_group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a Gazetteer to a GazetteerGroup."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#member_of_group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "member of group"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about
<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links a meta-Attestation to the Attestation it comments on or relates to.\n        Used with plato:has_meta_type to specify the nature of the relationship.\n\n        Example: A meta-attestation might assert that one source's geometry\n        attestation contradicts another source's geometry attestation for the\n        same SpatialEntity.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#meta_attestation_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "meta-attestation about"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The capacity in which the attested form occurs in the source. Should\n        point to a concept in a SKOS concept scheme. The starter concepts are:\n\n        - plato:Direct: the form refers to the SpatialEntity directly. The\n          default, and usually omitted.\n        - plato:InPersonalName: the form occurs only as an element of a\n          personal name, a surname or by-name such as 'Willelmus de\n          Bonestou'. This is the '(p)' of the place-name surveys, and it is\n          weaker evidence for the name's currency, and for the entity's\n          existence, than a direct attestation. Nothing else in the record\n          distinguishes Bonestou the hundred from de Bonestou the man.\n        - plato:InFieldName: the form survives only as an element of a later\n          minor name, such as a field name.\n\n        The editorially resolved 'ibidem' of the surveys is not an occurrence\n        context. It is a statement about the citation, and belongs on the\n        Citation as plato:attribution_status.\n\n        Not a certainty. A '(p)' attestation may be entirely certain as an\n        attestation; what differs is the kind of evidence it constitutes, and\n        folding that into a lower plato:certainty would discard the reason.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_context> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "occurrence context"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#partOf
<https://w3id.org/plato#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Dataset> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a Source to its parent Dataset."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#partOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "part of"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#promoted_from
<https://w3id.org/plato#promoted_from> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#promoted_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#promoted_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Candidate> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#promoted_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an IdentityRelation to the Candidate from which it was\n        promoted, preserving the algorithmic provenance. Optional:\n        identity relations can also be created directly by human\n        assertion without a prior Candidate.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#promoted_from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "promoted from"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relates_to
<https://w3id.org/plato#relates_to> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relates_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relates_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relates_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to a second SpatialEntity, asserting a relationship\n        between the Attestation's subject entity (via attests_about) and this\n        target entity. The semantic nature of the relationship is specified by\n        plato:has_relation_type, which references a RelationType authority.\n\n        Example: An attestation about Constantinople that relates_to the\n        Byzantine Empire with relation_type \"capital_of\" asserts that\n        \"Constantinople was the capital of the Byzantine Empire\".\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relates_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "relates to"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relative_qualifier
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_qualifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_qualifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:genid1 .
_:genid1 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:genid5 .
_:genid5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid4 .
_:genid4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid3 .
_:genid3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid2 .
