_:genid3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
_:genid4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
_:genid5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_qualifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_qualifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A controlled-vocabulary term describing the relative relationship\n        when bearing and distance are not applicable or not sufficient.\n        Should point to a concept in a SKOS concept scheme (e.g.\n        plato:Near, plato:Within, plato:Beyond, plato:UpstreamOf,\n        plato:BetweenXAndY, plato:DuringReignOf, plato:VariantOf).\n        Using URIs rather than free text enables machine reconciliation\n        across gazetteers that describe relativity differently.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_qualifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "relative qualifier"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relative_to
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_to> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:genid6 .
