_:genid14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#Period> .
_:genid15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
_:genid16 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links a facet node to its anchor entity, indicating that this\n        facet is defined relationally rather than absolutely. The anchor\n        is typically a SpatialEntity, Period, or another facet (Name, Timespan, etc.).\n\n        Common patterns:\n        - Spatial relativity: \"20km east of Nanjing\" (anchor is a SpatialEntity)\n        - Temporal relativity: \"during the reign of Justinian\" (anchor is a Period)\n        - Name relativity: \"also known as Rome\" (anchor is another Name)\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "relative to"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point
<https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        When this Source, as a document, was produced: the date of the\n        manuscript, the compilation of the cartulary, the publication of the\n        edition. Distinct from the Timespan an attestation asserts, which\n        dates the claim rather than the witness. An annal for 921 read in a\n        manuscript written c. 925 has an attested timespan of 921 and a\n        source timespan of c. 925. Reuses Timespan, so an approximate date\n        is start_earliest 915, end_latest 935, timespan_label 'c. 925'. The\n        same move as plato:has_timespan on a Period.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_timespan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "source timespan"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by
<https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#propertyChainAxiom> _:genid18 .
_:genid18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid17 .
_:genid17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:genid17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#cites> .
_:genid17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#has_citation> .
_:genid18 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Links an Attestation to the Authority (typically a Source or Dataset)\n        that grounds it. This provides the provenance chain for the attestation.\n\n        Semantically equivalent to PROV-O's prov:wasDerivedFrom, indicating the\n        authority is the origin of the attested knowledge. We don't use formal\n        rdfs:subPropertyOf to avoid importing PROV-O's domain/range constraints\n        which conflict with PLATO's class structure.\n\n        This is the direct form. Where the citation itself has something to\n        say (a page or folio, an attribution resolved from 'ibidem'), use\n        plato:has_citation to a Citation node that cites the Authority.\n        sourced_by is declared as the property chain has_citation o cites, so\n        a reasoner derives it from a Citation; data intended for consumers\n        without a reasoner should assert it directly as well.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sourced_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sourced by"@en .
