<https://w3id.org/plato#ccodes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country codes associated with this SpatialEntity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#ccodes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "country codes"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#certainty
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Epistemic certainty, from 0.0 (completely uncertain) to 1.0\n        (completely certain). On an Attestation it is the contributor's\n        confidence in the bundle as a whole. On a facet node (Name, Geometry,\n        Timespan, Type, PropertyValue) it is the confidence in that value\n        alone, and may differ from the attestation's overall certainty.\n        Certainty reflects the limits of evidence: better evidence could in\n        principle raise it. Distinct from fuzziness (the referent has no\n        sharp boundary) and from spatial_precision (how finely a location\n        is specified). No rdfs:domain, so it can qualify any node.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "certainty"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#certainty_note
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty_note> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty_note> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty_note> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Free-text explanation of the certainty assessment: quality of\n        evidence, degree of scholarly consensus, reliability of source\n        (e.g. 'manuscript partially illegible', 'coordinates extrapolated\n        from itinerary distances'). Applies wherever certainty does.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#certainty_note> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "certainty note"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#connection_metadata
<https://w3id.org/plato#connection_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#connection_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#connection_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#connection_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Structured metadata for network-type attestations. Can encode\n        information about trade goods, flow direction, capacity, frequency,\n        or other properties of network connections. Format is implementation-\n        specific (JSON recommended) but should be documented in the gazetteer's\n        metadata.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#connection_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "connection metadata"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation_string
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation_string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Free-text organizational affiliation when a structured Organization\n        entity is not available. Example: \"University of Pittsburgh,\n        Institute for Spatial History Innovation\"\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_affiliation_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "affiliation (string)"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Contact email address for the contributor. Useful for collaboration\n        and correspondence about contributed data.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_email> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "email"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_identifier
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Additional persistent identifier for the contributor. Can be used\n        for identifiers other than ORCID, such as:\n        - ISNI (International Standard Name Identifier)\n        - VIAF (Virtual International Authority File)\n        - Wikidata QID (for persons or organizations)\n        - Internal system identifiers\n\n        When using this property, specify the identifier type in the value\n        (e.g., \"ISNI:0000000121032683\" or \"VIAF:12345678\").\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contributor identifier"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The name of the contributor (person, team, or automated process).\n        For persons, should be the full name as preferred by the contributor.\n        For teams, the team name. For automated processes, a descriptive name.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contributor name"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_orcid
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_orcid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_orcid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_orcid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_orcid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        ORCID identifier for person contributors. Can be provided in two formats:\n\n        1. Compact format: 0000-0000-0000-0000 (sixteen digits in groups of four)\n        2. URI format: https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000 (preferred)\n\n        The URI format (https://orcid.org/...) is preferred and required for\n        proper linked data representation. ORCID is particular about always\n        including the https:// protocol and domain prefix.\n\n        While optional in the general ontology, specific implementations\n        (e.g., WHG) may require ORCID for person contributors to ensure\n        proper attribution and citation.\n\n        ORCID provides persistent identification for researchers, enabling\n        proper credit and reducing name ambiguity.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_orcid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ORCID"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_role
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_role> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Role of the contributor in the project or gazetteer. Examples:\n        'principal_investigator', 'data_curator', 'student_researcher',\n        'automated_process', 'external_contributor'. Helps understand the\n        context and authority of contributions.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contributor role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_url
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_url> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_url> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Contributor> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_url> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_url> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Website or profile URL for the contributor (personal website,\n        institutional page, project page, GitHub profile, etc.). Provides\n        additional context about the contributor's work and identity.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#contributor_url> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "contributor URL"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#created
<https://w3id.org/plato#created> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#created> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#created> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#created> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Timestamp when this attestation was created. This is the contribution\n        date, not the historical timespan being attested (use attests_timespan\n        for that).\n\n        Semantically equivalent to PROV-O's prov:generatedAtTime. We don't use\n        formal rdfs:subPropertyOf to avoid importing PROV-O constraints.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#created> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "created"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#edtf_string
<https://w3id.org/plato#edtf_string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#edtf_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#edtf_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#edtf_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Extended Date/Time Format (EDTF) representation of this timespan.\n        Provides standardized string encoding for interchange with systems\n        using EDTF. Optional but recommended for interoperability with library\n        and archival systems. Example: '1453-05-29/1453-05-29' or '1450~/1453~'\n        for approximate dates.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#edtf_string> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EDTF string"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#end_earliest
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The earliest possible end date for this timespan. Together with\n        end_latest, defines the uncertainty range for when the interval ended.\n        May be null for unknown or deliberately open-end intervals.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "end earliest"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#end_latest
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_latest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The latest possible end date for this timespan. For certain dates,\n        this equals end_earliest. For uncertain dates, defines the end of\n        the uncertainty range for when the interval ended.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "end latest"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#end_precision
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_precision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Temporal granularity of the end bound. Values: 'year', 'decade',\n        'century', 'era', 'geological_period'.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#end_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "end precision"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier
<https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The stable, persistent identifier for this SpatialEntity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#entity_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identifier"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Ontological fuzziness: a measure of how inherently vague or\n        indeterminate the facet's referent is, from 0.0 (crisp, sharply\n        bounded) to 1.0 (maximally vague). Distinct from certainty:\n        fuzziness is a property of the thing itself, not of our knowledge\n        of it. A regional boundary that was never precisely defined has\n        high fuzziness regardless of how much evidence we have.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fuzziness"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness_note
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness_note> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness_note> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness_note> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Free-text explanation of the nature of ontological fuzziness\n        (e.g. 'regional boundary was never formally demarcated',\n        'name used inconsistently across contemporary sources',\n        'transition was gradual rather than a discrete event').\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#fuzziness_note> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fuzziness note"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_status
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_status> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Gazetteer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Publication status: 'draft' or 'published'."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#gazetteer_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "status"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#generated_at
<https://w3id.org/plato#generated_at> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#generated_at> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Candidate> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#generated_at> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#generated_at> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "generated at"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#geo_json
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_json> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        GeoJSON representation of the geometry. Used for web mapping\n        applications and LPF export. Should be a valid GeoJSON geometry\n        object (not a Feature or FeatureCollection).\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "geometry GeoJSON"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#asWKT> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#hull
<https://w3id.org/plato#hull> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_at
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_at> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_at> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_at> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_asserted_at> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "asserted at"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_basis
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_basis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_basis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_basis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_basis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Free-text explanation of the evidence or reasoning supporting\n        this identity assertion (e.g. 'coordinates within 500m and\n        name forms are cognate', 'identified by contributor during\n        reconciliation review', 'confirmed via TGN cross-reference').\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_basis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identity basis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_certainty
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_certainty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Confidence in the identity assertion, from 0.0 to 1.0. This is\n        the epistemic certainty of the asserter, distinct from identity_type\n        which describes the semantic nature of the relationship.\n        A closeMatch can have high certainty ('I'm confident these are\n        close but not exact') and an exactMatch can have low certainty\n        ('I think they're identical but I'm not sure').\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_certainty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identity certainty"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#IdentityRelation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The semantic strength of the identity assertion:\n        'exactMatch'  — the two SpatialEntities are unambiguously the same entity.\n        'closeMatch'  — the two SpatialEntities are believed to be the same entity\n                        but with some residual ambiguity (e.g. differing\n                        granularity, overlapping but not identical scope).\n        'related'     — the two SpatialEntities are closely associated but may not\n                        be strictly identical (e.g. a settlement and its\n                        administrative district, or successive phases of\n                        a site that might or might not constitute continuity).\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#identity_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "identity type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#inverse_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#inverse_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#inverse_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#inverse_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#inverse_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inverse label (e.g. 'has_capital')."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#inverse_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "inverse label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#ipa
<https://w3id.org/plato#ipa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#ipa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#ipa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#ipa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        International Phonetic Alphabet representation of the name's\n        pronunciation. Enables phonetic search and comparison across scripts\n        and languages.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#ipa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IPA"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#language
<https://w3id.org/plato#language> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#language> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#language> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#language> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        BCP 47 language tag for this name (e.g., 'ar' for Arabic, 'zh-Hans'\n        for Simplified Chinese). Recommended: use ISO 639-3 three-letter codes\n        within BCP 47 for better granularity (e.g., 'ara', 'cmn').\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#language> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "language"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#licence
<https://w3id.org/plato#licence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#licence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Dataset> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#licence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#licence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "licence"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#locator
<https://w3id.org/plato#locator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#locator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Citation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#locator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#locator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Where in the cited work the evidence sits: 'p. 412', 'f. 12v', 'Table\n        VI, col. 3, row 88', 's.v. Athlone', 'no. xix'. An uninterpreted\n        string, deliberately: sources locate themselves inconsistently, and\n        normalising the value would destroy exactly the information it is\n        there to carry. The same position and shape as PeriodO's source\n        locator.\n\n        A property of this citation, not of the source: one Source for a\n        printed gazetteer, a different locator on each attestation drawn\n        from it. Not to be confused with the spatial sense of 'locator' in\n        the plato:geometry_role comment, a proxy point standing in for an\n        entity.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#locator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "locator"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#modified
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Timestamp when this attestation was last modified. Enables tracking\n        of editorial changes and versioning.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#modified> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "modified"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Vector embedding for phonetic similarity search. Typically a\n        256-dimensional vector generated from the name's phonetic form,\n        enabling fuzzy matching and transliteration-variant detection.\n        Format is implementation-specific but should be documented in\n        gazetteer metadata. WHG v4 uses Symphonym embeddings.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_embedding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "name embedding"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#name_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        What the name denotes. The list is open: 'toponym' (place name),\n        'chrononym' (period or era name), 'ethnonym' (people or ethnic\n        group), 'demonym' (inhabitants), 'odonym' (street or road name) and\n        'hydronym' (water body) are the starter values, and a project may\n        add others ('oronym', 'hagionym') provided it documents them in its\n        gazetteer metadata. Multiple types are possible (a name that\n        functions as both toponym and ethnonym). plato.schema.json carries\n        the same open list; earlier releases closed it there, and the two\n        serialisations now agree.\n\n        This classifies the referent, not the status of the form. Whether a\n        string is an attested spelling, an editorial headword or a derived\n        search form is a property of the attestation (plato:form_status),\n        because the same string can have a different status in different\n        attestations.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#name_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "name type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#namespace
<https://w3id.org/plato#namespace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#namespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#SpatialEntity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#namespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#namespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The authority namespace for this SpatialEntity (e.g. 'geonames', 'wikidata',\n        'tgn', 'osm', 'pleiades', 'whg'). Authority-sourced SpatialEntities carry\n        their origin namespace; contributed SpatialEntities that cannot be linked to\n        any authority receive the 'whg' namespace.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#namespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "namespace"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#notes
<https://w3id.org/plato#notes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#notes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#notes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#notes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Free-text notes providing additional context about this attestation.\n        Can include transcriptions, translations, editorial comments, or\n        other information that doesn't fit structured fields.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#notes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "notes"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_count
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_count> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_count> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_count> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_count> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The number of times the attested form occurs in the cited source or\n        passage: the '(3 X)' of a place-name survey. A count of occurrences\n        of the form in this source, not of independent sources. It belongs to\n        the attestation, not to the Name, which may occur elsewhere.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#occurrence_count> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "occurrence count"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#open_end
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_end> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_end> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_end> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_end> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Boolean flag indicating that the end of this interval is deliberately\n        unspecified (not merely unknown). True for ongoing periods like 'Modern\n        era (1800-present)' or situations where the end does not exist. Aligns\n        with PeriodO's OpenEndInterval.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_end> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "open end"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#open_start
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_start> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_start> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_start> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_start> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Boolean flag indicating that the start of this interval is deliberately\n        unspecified (not merely unknown). True for intervals like 'everything\n        before 1453' or 'prehistory until...'. Distinct from null start_earliest,\n        which indicates unknown start. Aligns with PeriodO's OpenBeginningInterval.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#open_start> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "open start"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#period_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Period> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Human-readable label for this period (e.g., 'Byzantine period',\n        'Han Dynasty', 'Early Bronze Age'). Distinct from authority_title,\n        which may be more formal.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "period label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#period_periodo_uri
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Period> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Link to a PeriodO period definition for this Period authority.\n        When present, indicates this Period aligns with a standardized PeriodO\n        definition. The PeriodO record provides authoritative temporal bounds,\n        spatial extent, and cultural context. Example: 'https://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p06v8w4rb38'\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#period_periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PeriodO URI"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#periodo_uri
<https://w3id.org/plato#periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Link to a PeriodO period definition (https://perio.do/). When a timespan\n        corresponds to a standardized period in PeriodO, this property enables\n        alignment and allows PLATO to inherit PeriodO's temporal bounds, spatial\n        coverage, and cultural context. Example: 'https://n2t.net/ark:/99152/p06v8w4rb38'\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#periodo_uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PeriodO URI"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#precision_km
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_km> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_km> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_km> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_km> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Uncertainty radius in kilometers. For point geometries, indicates\n        how far the true location might be from the stated coordinates.\n        For polygons, indicates boundary uncertainty. Can be multiple values\n        for heterogeneous geometries.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_km> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "precision in kilometers"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#precision_value
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_value> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Numeric precision indicator in years. For example, a decade-level\n        precision would have value 10, century-level would be 100. Enables\n        computational comparison of precision across timespans.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#precision_value> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "precision value"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#property_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Human-readable label for the property (e.g. 'population')."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "property label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#property_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        URI of the property in an external vocabulary — a Wikidata property,\n        a CIDOC-CRM property, or a project vocabulary term (e.g.\n        <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Property:P1082> for population).\n        Keeping the vocabulary external rather than enumerating attributes in\n        this ontology is what allows the model to carry attributes it has\n        never heard of.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#property_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "property type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#publisher
<https://w3id.org/plato#publisher> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Dataset> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#publisher> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "publisher"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Valid subject type for this relation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "domain constraint"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Forward label for the relationship (e.g. 'capital_of')."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "relation label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relation_range
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_range> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Valid object type for this relation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relation_range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "range constraint"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relative_bearing
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_bearing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_bearing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_bearing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Compass bearing from the anchor, in degrees (0–360).\n        Primarily used for relative geometries: '90' means east of\n        the anchor. May carry its own certainty or fuzziness.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_bearing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "bearing"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#relative_distance
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_distance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_distance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_distance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Distance from the anchor, in metres. Primarily used for\n        relative geometries. May carry its own certainty or fuzziness.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#relative_distance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "distance"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point
<https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#romanized
<https://w3id.org/plato#romanized> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#romanized> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#romanized> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#romanized> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Romanized (Latin-script) form of the name for searchability and\n        display in contexts requiring ASCII. Should specify transliteration\n        system used via plato:transliteration_system.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#romanized> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "romanized"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#script
<https://w3id.org/plato#script> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#script> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#script> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#script> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        ISO 15924 script code (e.g., 'Arab' for Arabic script, 'Latn' for\n        Latin script, 'Hant' for Traditional Han characters). Important for\n        names that may appear in multiple scripts.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#script> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "script"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#sequence
<https://w3id.org/plato#sequence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sequence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sequence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sequence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Ordering index for attestations in routes or itineraries. Defines\n        the position of this attestation in an ordered sequence. Used when\n        the SpatialEntity being attested (via attests_about) is a Route or Itinerary.\n        Lower numbers come first in the sequence.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#sequence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sequence"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#similarity_score
<https://w3id.org/plato#similarity_score> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#similarity_score> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Candidate> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#similarity_score> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#similarity_score> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "similarity score"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#source_crs
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_crs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_crs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_crs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_crs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Original coordinate reference system. Typically 'EPSG:4326' (WGS84),\n        but may reference historical or custom CRS identifiers for historical\n        maps. Enables proper interpretation of coordinate values.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_crs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "source CRS"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#source_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:genid19 .
_:genid19 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:genid21 .
_:genid21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:genid20 .
_:genid20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:genid20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#Type> .
_:genid20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
_:genid21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid19 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The original label as given in the contributing source, before\n        vocabulary mapping. For a structured PropertyValue this preserves the\n        unparsed original — 'Monday after Whitsun, 3 days' — which is what a\n        future reader will want to check against the document.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#source_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "source label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Period> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Geographic or cultural region to which this period applies.\n        Free text or URI to a place/region. Useful because periods like\n        'Medieval' have different temporal bounds in different regions.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "spatial coverage"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_precision
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_precision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Geometry> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Precision qualifier for this geometry: 'exact' (surveyed or GPS),\n        'approximate' (estimated from maps or descriptions), 'uncertain'\n        (multiple possible locations), 'historical_approximate' (based on\n        historical sources with inherent imprecision). Multiple values\n        possible for heterogeneous geometries.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#spatial_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "spatial precision"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#start_earliest
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The earliest possible start date for this timespan. Together with\n        start_latest, defines the uncertainty range for when the interval began.\n        Use ISO 8601 format (e.g., '1453-05-29') or integer year for year-level\n        precision. May be null for unknown or deliberately open-beginning intervals.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_earliest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "start earliest"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The latest possible start date for this timespan. For certain dates,\n        this equals start_earliest. For uncertain dates, defines the end of\n        the uncertainty range for when the interval began.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_latest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "start latest"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Temporal granularity of the start bound. Values: 'year', 'decade',\n        'century', 'era', 'geological_period'. This describes the resolution\n        of the date specification, distinct from certainty (which describes\n        the confidence in that specification).\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#start_precision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "start precision"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#timespan_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#timespan_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#timespan_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Timespan> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#timespan_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#timespan_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Human-readable label for this timespan (e.g., 'Byzantine period',\n        'Early Bronze Age', 'Ming Dynasty'). Particularly useful for named\n        periods referenced across multiple attestations.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#timespan_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "timespan label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#toponym
<https://w3id.org/plato#toponym> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#toponym> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#toponym> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#toponym> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#toponym> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The name string itself in its original script. This is the primary\n        property of a Name entity. Required for all Name instances.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#toponym> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "toponym"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#transliteration_system
<https://w3id.org/plato#transliteration_system> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#transliteration_system> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Name> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#transliteration_system> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#transliteration_system> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The transliteration/romanization system used (e.g., 'Pinyin' for\n        Chinese, 'BGN/PCGN' for Arabic, 'ISO 259' for Hebrew, 'Hepburn' for\n        Japanese). Enables proper interpretation and comparison of romanized\n        forms.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#transliteration_system> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "transliteration system"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#type_identifier
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Type> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "URI or identifier in a controlled vocabulary (e.g. AAT)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_identifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "type identifier"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#type_label
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_label> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#Type> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Human-readable label for this type."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#type_label> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "type label"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#value_datatype
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_datatype> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Datatype of the literal value (e.g. xsd:integer, xsd:decimal, xsd:string)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "value datatype"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#value_json
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_json> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A structured value serialised as JSON, whose shape is declared by\n        plato:value_type. Use plato:value_literal instead for scalar values.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_json> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "structured value"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        The value, where it is a literal: a number, a string, a date. Use\n        plato:value_json instead where the value is structured.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_literal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "value"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#value_type
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        URI declaring the shape of a structured value, so that a consumer can\n        tell whether it understands the value before attempting to read it.\n        Omitted for literal values.\n\n        Not every attribute a source states is scalar. A market's trading day\n        — 'the Monday after Whitsun, for three days' — is a recurrence rule\n        anchored to a moveable feast, and flattening it to a string would\n        reproduce the loss this class exists to prevent. The ontology stays\n        agnostic about such shapes: it records which shape is in use and\n        leaves the definition to the vocabulary that owns it.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "value type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/plato#PropertyValue> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        URI of the unit of measurement, where the value has one — a QUDT unit\n        or a Wikidata unit item. Omitted for counts and dimensionless values.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#value_unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "value unit"@en .
