<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
# 
# http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation
<https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A bundle of evidence asserting that a particular SpatialEntity had a particular\n        Name, Geometry, Type, or combination thereof, during a particular\n        Timespan, according to a particular Authority. The Attestation node\n        carries only metadata; its semantic content is defined entirely by its\n        outgoing relationships.\n\n        IMPORTANT: Attestations are document nodes in the graph, not edges.\n        They are instances of plato:Attestation (a class), not instances of\n        owl:ObjectProperty. This design enables meta-attestations and full\n        provenance tracking.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Attestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Attestation"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/plato#Authority
<https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/plato#Authority> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointUnionOf> _:genid26 .
