<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Well-Known Text representation of the geometry, following OGC/ISO\n        standards. Used for GeoSPARQL queries and RDF serialization.\n        Supports Point, LineString, Polygon, MultiPoint, MultiLineString,\n        MultiPolygon.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#geo_wkt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "geometry WKT"@en .
# 
<https://w3id.org/plato#hull> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        Convex hull of the geometry as WKT Polygon. Used for quick spatial\n        filtering before more expensive exact geometry operations. Optional\n        but recommended for complex geometries.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#hull> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "convex hull"@en .
# 
<https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n        A single representative point (centroid, label point, or best\n        estimate) for spatial indexing and distance queries. Stored as WKT\n        Point. Required for all geometries to enable spatial search.\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/plato#repr_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "representative point"@en .
